candidate can expect on the EMT exam ranges from 70 to 120. Each exam will have between 60 and 110 \"real-world\" items that count toward the final score. The exam will also have 10 pilot questions that will not affect the final score. The maximum time to complete the exam is 2 hours.\n\nThis app offers subjects aligned to the scope of the exam, as well as thousands of questions similar to the exam questions with full answer explanations. Included:\n\n- Airway, breathing and ventilation.\n- Cardiology and resuscitation.\n- Trauma; medical treatment.\n- Obstetrics/gynecology.\n- EMS Operations.\nKey Features:\n- Comprehensive set of EMT practice questions: with detailed explanations and images (latest version).\n- Multiple advanced study modes: feel free to choose the most effective study mode for your current stage.\n- Professional performance analysis system: track your performance for each practice session and analyze it by subject.\n- Easy to use practice review: you can go back to the last dozens of practice sessions and retake the test.\n-------------------------------------------\n\nPremium Subscription\n\n-------------------------------------------\n\nPayment will be charged to your credit card through your iTunes account at confirmation of purchase. Subscription renews automatically unless canceled at least 24 hours prior to the end of the subscription period.\n\nThere is no increase in price when renewing.\n\nSubscriptions can be managed and auto-renewal turned off in Account Settings in iTunes after purchase. Once purchased, refunds will not be provided for any unused portion of the term.\n\nThese prices are for United States customers. Pricing in other countries may vary and actual charges may be converted to your local currency depending on the country of residence.\n\nPrivacy Policy and Terms of Use:\nhttps://sites.google.com/view/metawisdom/%E9%A6%96%E9%A1%B5\n\n\n","rating":4.6,"ratingCount":"5","buttonAction":{"title":"Get","presentationStyle":[],"ac